/* =====================================================================
   Torrent 2000 -- "CCCP" skin, NORMAL variant  (v3 rebuild, from zero)

   Not a real OS, so there is no screenshot to trace: the reference is real
   Soviet civil-war-era propaganda-poster art (Rodchenko / El Lissitzky /
   Dmitry Moor school) -- flat silkscreened color fields, thick square-cut
   ink borders around thin-hairline picture frames, bold sans display type.
   No gradients, no soft shading, no rounded corners.

   PALETTE -- measured from 4 real posters (Wikimedia Commons, public
   domain / PD-old), pixel-sampled with PIL: red/black/cream classified by
   channel heuristic on a downsampled copy (avoids anti-aliased-edge noise
   from a single hand-picked coordinate), then the RED bucket specifically
   run through a 3-means numpy k-means pass per image (dominant cluster
   kept) so one JPEG-compression fleck can't skew a plain median. See
   scratchpad CHARTE_CCCP.md for the full method and per-image numbers.

     measured red    -> #D95231  (k-means avg across 3 posters: "Krasny
                         Podarok" rocket-red, Moor's "Have You Volunteered"
                         tunic-red, Lissitzky's red wedge -- all three
                         within ~10/255 per channel of each other, a tight
                         cluster). A 4th poster ("Join the Red Army") was
                         measured too but its flag-red reads distinctly
                         pinker/lighter (#DD6573) -- a different print run,
                         not the same pigment convention -- so it was kept
                         out of the red average and used for cream/paper
                         context only, same call the v2 charte already made.
     measured board   -> #2A2A28  (avg of the same 3 posters' black-ground
                         clusters -- notably lighter than a naive "pure
                         black" guess: aged print ink scans as a warm dark
                         charcoal, not #000)
     measured cream   -> #EADFC8  (avg of all 4 posters' aged-paper
                         clusters) -- within 8/255 per channel of the title
                         bar's ALREADY-FIXED caption text color #F2E4C4
                         (theme_manager.py), confirming that fixed value
                         belongs to the same parchment family rather than
                         contradicting it, so it's reused as-is below.

   PROPORTIONS -- this rebuild's actual change from v2, not just refreshed
   hex codes. v2 used a near-uniform 2px border almost everywhere, which
   reads as "a dark theme with red accents," not as these posters. Measured
   two real ratios on the Moor poster (2650x3750, the highest-res, cleanest
   reference) that v2 never extracted:
     - the poster's own hairline picture-frame is ~8px thick on a 3750px-
       tall sheet (~1:470) and only ~5% of the bold headline lettering's
       cap-height (~158px) alongside it -- i.e. real hairline vs bold is a
       DRAMATIC weight contrast, not a subtle one.
     - the bold headline's letter-strokes themselves run ~18-19px thick on
       that same ~78px cap-height (measured on the "KRASNYY PODAROK"
       headline, poster 02) -- ~23% of cap-height, genuinely heavy type.
     - the black text-band a headline sits inside runs ~3x the headline's
       own cap-height -- structure in these posters is bold color BLOCKS,
       not thick lines.
   Raw pixel counts from a 3750px scan don't transfer to a 9pt control, so
   what carries over is the RATIO: a stark hairline/bold contrast. Applied
   here as three consistent tiers instead of one flat width:
     1px  hairline  -- every control's resting-state border
     2px  emphasis  -- hover / focus / pressed / selected states
     4px  bold      -- the few singular structural accents a poster would
                        render as a color block, not a rule: QGroupBox's
                        top band, QTabBar's selected-tab underline, the
                        propaganda-panel divider
   Corner radius stays 0px everywhere, echoing window_corner_radius=0 for
   CCCP in theme_manager.py (square window chrome -> square controls).

   ICON -- QCheckBox's checkmark is an original glyph (assets/icons/cccp/
   checkmark.png, drawn from scratch as two filled flat-cut polygons in
   PIL/ImageDraw, not traced from any existing OS icon) sized to that same
   ~23%-of-height stroke weight instead of the thin shared default tick.

   CURSOR -- the mouse pointer over the window's non-text chrome is an
   original arrow glyph too (assets/cursors/cccp/arrow.png, same from-
   scratch PIL/ImageDraw origin as the checkmark, never traced from a real
   OS cursor). Kept a plain functional arrow silhouette -- readability over
   theming for something the eye tracks constantly -- but recolored to this
   theme's own parchment-on-red palette (measured cream fill #EADFC8, ink-
   line red outline #D95231) instead of the stock black/white system arrow.
   Hotspot is (4, 3): the drawn tip pixel, i.e. where the actual click
   lands, measured directly off the 32x32 PNG. One image serves all three
   appearance variants below -- a real system pointer doesn't reshape
   itself for dark mode either, and cream-on-red reads fine against every
   variant's background here. Scoped to QMainWindow/centralWidget/QDialog,
   QGroupBox, QTabBar and the table/tree backgrounds only -- deliberately
   NOT a blanket QWidget rule, so QLineEdit/QComboBox keep the native
   I-beam and every already-clickable control keeps its own affordance.

   TOKENS (hex, named)
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
     bg               #161616   canvas the poster board sits on -- reads as
                                 the wall behind the mounted poster, darker
                                 than the board itself, not poster-measured
     surface          #2A2A28   panel / card -- measured poster board, used
                                 directly
     border           #EADFC8   parchment ink-line -- measured poster cream
     text             #F2E4C4   parchment cream -- ALREADY FIXED (title bar
                                 caption text, theme_manager.py); measured
                                 cream (#EADFC8) confirms the same family
     text-muted       #9F9888   dulled parchment -- measured cream at ~68%
                                 HSV value (same hue/warmth, just dimmer)
     accent (red)     #D95231   primary interactive red -- measured poster
                                 red, used directly
     accent-hover     #D4AF37   gold -- ALREADY FIXED (title bar hover gold,
                                 theme_manager.py). Every hover state here
                                 resolves red-becomes-gold, same as hovering
                                 the real caption buttons.
     danger           #A31515   destructive-action red -- ALREADY FIXED
                                 (title bar close/minmax fill,
                                 theme_manager.py) -- the one button allowed
                                 to BE red instead of merely bordered by it.

   Utility shades (not part of the named palette, purely structural -- a
   disabled control or an inset field has no equivalent in 1920s silkscreen
   art, these are invented, not measured):
     inset            #0D0D0D   recessed field background
     hover-surface    #35352F   lightened board, generic hover fill
     alt-row          #1A1A1A   table alternating row
     disabled-border  #3A3A3A   deliberately neutral, not warm -- a
                                 disabled control should read "switched
                                 off," not a dimmer parchment tone
     disabled-text    #6E6E6E

   ANIMATION -- honest gap, not attempted here. QSS has no transition/
   animation properties at all (unlike CSS3): a hover can't ease, it can
   only snap. The 1px-to-2px border jump above is the closest static
   substitute -- a discrete weight change reads as "this became active"
   even without motion. A real transition (the border widening, or the
   danger button's gold hover fading in) would need QPropertyAnimation in
   Python driving a custom paintEvent or an animated QGraphicsEffect, which
   is out of scope for a stylesheet-only pass.

   The title bar (solid red caption, hammer-and-sickle close button) is NOT
   drawn by this stylesheet -- see ui/widgets/app_title_bar.py and
   ui/theme/theme_manager.py. Two theme-specific mechanics live outside QSS
   entirely: downloading is blocked while this theme is active
   (engine/session_manager.py) and sharing counts for 3x toward the level
   (stats/leveling.py).
   ===================================================================== */

* {
    font-family: "Arial", "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    font-size: 9pt;
}

QMainWindow, QWidget#centralWidget, QDialog {
    background-color: #161616;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    cursor: url(theme:cursors/cccp/arrow.png) 4 3;
}

QWidget {
    background-color: #161616;
    color: #F2E4C4;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------- Tabs */

QTabWidget::pane {
    border: 1px solid #EADFC8;
    background-color: #161616;
    top: -1px;
}

QTabWidget#mainTabs::pane {
    border-top: none;
    top: 0px;
}

QTabBar::tab {
    background-color: #2A2A28;
    border: 1px solid #EADFC8;
    border-bottom: none;
    border-radius: 0px;
    padding: 5px 16px;
    margin-right: 1px;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    font-weight: bold;
}

QTabBar::tab:hover:!selected {
    background-color: #35352F;
    color: #D4AF37;
    border-color: #D4AF37;
    border-width: 2px;
}

QTabBar::tab:selected {
    background-color: #161616;
    border-color: #EADFC8;
    border-bottom: 4px solid #D95231;
    margin-top: 0px;
    color: #D95231;
}

QTabBar::tab:!selected {
    margin-top: 2px;
}

QTabBar::tab:disabled {
    color: #6E6E6E;
    border-color: #3A3A3A;
}

QTabBar::tab:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #D4AF37;
    outline-offset: -3px;
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------ GroupBox */

QGroupBox {
    border: 1px solid #EADFC8;
    border-top: 4px solid #D95231;
    border-radius: 0px;
    margin-top: 10px;
    padding-top: 10px;
    background-color: #2A2A28;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #D95231;
    cursor: url(theme:cursors/cccp/arrow.png) 4 3;
}

QTabBar {
    cursor: url(theme:cursors/cccp/arrow.png) 4 3;
}

QGroupBox::title {
    subcontrol-origin: margin;
    left: 10px;
    top: -2px;
    padding: 0 6px;
    background-color: #2A2A28;
    color: #D95231;
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------- Buttons */

QPushButton {
    background-color: #2A2A28;
    border: 1px solid #EADFC8;
    border-radius: 0px;
    padding: 4px 12px;
    min-height: 18px;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    font-weight: bold;
}

QPushButton:hover:!pressed {
    background-color: #35352F;
    border: 2px solid #D4AF37;
    color: #D4AF37;
}

QPushButton:pressed {
    background-color: #0D0D0D;
    border: 2px solid #D95231;
    color: #D95231;
}

QPushButton:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #D4AF37;
    outline-offset: 2px;
}

QPushButton:default {
    border-width: 2px;
    border-color: #D95231;
    color: #FFFFFF;
}

QPushButton:disabled {
    background-color: #2A2A28;
    border: 1px solid #3A3A3A;
    color: #6E6E6E;
}

/* The one button allowed to BE red instead of merely bordered by it --
   removing a torrent is exactly the kind of decisive action this theme's
   red accent is reserved for. Fill matches the real title bar's close/
   minmax button color exactly (see theme_manager.py). */
QPushButton#dangerButton {
    background-color: #A31515;
    border: 1px solid #EADFC8;
    border-radius: 0px;
    padding: 2px 10px;
    min-height: 16px;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    font-weight: bold;
}

QPushButton#dangerButton:hover:!pressed {
    background-color: #D4AF37;
    border: 2px solid #F2E4C4;
    color: #161616;
}

QPushButton#dangerButton:pressed {
    background-color: #6E0E0E;
    border: 2px solid #EADFC8;
    color: #F2E4C4;
}

QPushButton#dangerButton:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #F2E4C4;
    outline-offset: 2px;
}

QPushButton#dangerButton:disabled {
    background-color: #3A1414;
    border: 1px solid #3A3A3A;
    color: #6E6E6E;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------- Text input */

QLineEdit, QSpinBox, QAbstractSpinBox {
    background-color: #0D0D0D;
    border: 1px solid #3A3A3A;
    border-radius: 0px;
    padding: 2px 4px;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    selection-background-color: #D95231;
    selection-color: #F2E4C4;
}

QLineEdit:hover, QSpinBox:hover, QAbstractSpinBox:hover {
    border: 2px solid #D95231;
}

QLineEdit:focus, QSpinBox:focus, QAbstractSpinBox:focus {
    border: 2px solid #D4AF37;
    outline: 2px solid #D4AF37;
    outline-offset: 1px;
}

QLineEdit:disabled, QSpinBox:disabled, QAbstractSpinBox:disabled {
    background-color: #161616;
    border: 1px solid #3A3A3A;
    color: #6E6E6E;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::up-button, QAbstractSpinBox::down-button {
    subcontrol-origin: border;
    width: 16px;
    background-color: #2A2A28;
    border-left: 1px solid #3A3A3A;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::up-button {
    subcontrol-position: top right;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #3A3A3A;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::up-button:hover, QAbstractSpinBox::down-button:hover {
    background-color: #35352F;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::down-button {
    subcontrol-position: bottom right;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::up-arrow {
    width: 0;
    height: 0;
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
    border-right: 3px solid transparent;
    border-bottom: 4px solid #F2E4C4;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::down-arrow {
    width: 0;
    height: 0;
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
    border-right: 3px solid transparent;
    border-top: 4px solid #F2E4C4;
}

QAbstractSpinBox::up-arrow:disabled, QAbstractSpinBox::down-arrow:disabled {
    border-bottom-color: #6E6E6E;
    border-top-color: #6E6E6E;
}

/* -------------------------------------------------------------- Combo */

QComboBox {
    background-color: #0D0D0D;
    border: 1px solid #3A3A3A;
    border-radius: 0px;
    padding: 2px 4px;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    selection-background-color: #D95231;
    selection-color: #F2E4C4;
}

QComboBox:hover {
    border: 2px solid #D95231;
}

QComboBox:focus {
    border: 2px solid #D4AF37;
    outline: 2px solid #D4AF37;
    outline-offset: 1px;
}

QComboBox:disabled {
    background-color: #161616;
    border: 1px solid #3A3A3A;
    color: #6E6E6E;
}

QComboBox::drop-down {
    subcontrol-origin: padding;
    subcontrol-position: right;
    width: 20px;
    background-color: #2A2A28;
    border-left: 1px solid #3A3A3A;
}

QComboBox::drop-down:hover {
    background-color: #35352F;
}

QComboBox::down-arrow {
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    image: none;
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
    border-right: 3px solid transparent;
    border-top: 4px solid #F2E4C4;
}

QComboBox::down-arrow:disabled {
    border-top: 4px solid #6E6E6E;
}

/* Popup list -- the currently-selected/current item must never end up
   rendering with text the same color as its own background (the known
   Windows-7-family bug this rebuild must not repeat). selection-background-
   color/selection-color is declared on BOTH QComboBox itself and the popup
   view: QComboBox's own declaration is what the automated offscreen test
   harness renders from when the popup first opens with no live compositor;
   the view-level declaration is what a real desktop session paints from.
   Either mechanism alone was seen to silently no-op in one context or the
   other during this rebuild's verification pass, so both are kept -- not
   redundant, each covers a different render path. Verified by rendering
   the popup offscreen to PNG: text and fill are never the same color in
   any state below. */
QComboBox QAbstractItemView {
    background-color: #0D0D0D;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    border: 2px solid #D95231;
    outline: none;
    padding: 2px;
    selection-background-color: #D95231;
    selection-color: #F2E4C4;
}

QComboBox QAbstractItemView::item {
    padding: 4px 8px;
    min-height: 20px;
    background-color: #0D0D0D;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    border: none;
}

QComboBox QAbstractItemView::item:hover {
    background-color: #D95231;
    color: #F2E4C4;
}

QComboBox QAbstractItemView::item:selected {
    background-color: #D95231;
    color: #F2E4C4;
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------ Checkbox */

QCheckBox {
    color: #F2E4C4;
    spacing: 6px;
}

QCheckBox:disabled {
    color: #6E6E6E;
}

QCheckBox::indicator {
    width: 13px;
    height: 13px;
    background-color: #0D0D0D;
    border: 1px solid #3A3A3A;
}

QCheckBox::indicator:hover {
    border: 2px solid #D4AF37;
}

QCheckBox::indicator:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #D4AF37;
    outline-offset: 1px;
}

QCheckBox::indicator:checked {
    background-color: #D95231;
    border: 1px solid #D95231;
    image: url(theme:icons/cccp/checkmark.png);
}

QCheckBox::indicator:checked:hover {
    background-color: #D4AF37;
    border: 2px solid #D4AF37;
}

QCheckBox::indicator:disabled {
    background-color: #2A2A28;
    border: 1px solid #3A3A3A;
}

QCheckBox::indicator:checked:disabled {
    background-color: #6E6E6E;
    border: 1px solid #3A3A3A;
}

/* -------------------------------------------------------------- Slider */

QSlider::groove:horizontal {
    height: 4px;
    background-color: #3A3A3A;
    border: 1px solid #0D0D0D;
}

QSlider::groove:horizontal:disabled {
    background-color: #2A2A28;
}

QSlider::handle:horizontal {
    width: 14px;
    margin: -6px 0;
    background-color: #D95231;
    border: 2px solid #EADFC8;
}

QSlider::handle:horizontal:hover {
    background-color: #D4AF37;
    border: 2px solid #F2E4C4;
}

QSlider::handle:horizontal:pressed {
    background-color: #D4AF37;
    border: 2px solid #FFFFFF;
}

QSlider::handle:horizontal:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #D4AF37;
    outline-offset: 1px;
}

QSlider::handle:horizontal:disabled {
    background-color: #6E6E6E;
    border: 1px solid #3A3A3A;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------- Tables and trees */

QTableWidget, QTreeWidget {
    background-color: #0D0D0D;
    alternate-background-color: #1A1A1A;
    gridline-color: #3A3A3A;
    border: 1px solid #3A3A3A;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    selection-background-color: #D95231;
    selection-color: #F2E4C4;
    outline: none;
    cursor: url(theme:cursors/cccp/arrow.png) 4 3;
}

QTableWidget::item, QTreeWidget::item {
    padding: 2px;
}

QTableWidget::item:hover, QTreeWidget::item:hover {
    background-color: #2A1414;
}

QTableWidget::item:selected, QTreeWidget::item:selected {
    background-color: #D95231;
    color: #F2E4C4;
}

QHeaderView::section {
    background-color: #2A2A28;
    border: 1px solid #3A3A3A;
    padding: 3px 6px;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #D95231;
}

QHeaderView::section:hover {
    color: #D4AF37;
    border-color: #D4AF37;
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------- ListBox */

QListWidget {
    background-color: #0D0D0D;
    border: 1px solid #3A3A3A;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    outline: none;
}

QListWidget::item {
    padding: 4px 6px;
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
}

QListWidget::item:hover {
    background-color: #2A1414;
    border-left: 3px solid #D4AF37;
}

QListWidget::item:selected {
    background-color: #D95231;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    border-left: 3px solid #D4AF37;
}

QListWidget::item:selected:!active {
    background-color: #6E0E0E;
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ Menu */
/* Context menus (right-click on the Downloads/Share tables) need to look
   like part of the same poster, not fall back to native Windows chrome. */

QMenu {
    background-color: #2A2A28;
    border: 1px solid #EADFC8;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    padding: 3px;
}

QMenu::item {
    background-color: transparent;
    padding: 5px 24px 5px 16px;
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
}

QMenu::item:selected {
    background-color: #D95231;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    border-left: 3px solid #D4AF37;
}

QMenu::item:disabled {
    color: #6E6E6E;
}

QMenu::separator {
    height: 2px;
    background-color: #D4AF37;
    margin: 4px 8px;
}

QMenu::icon {
    padding-left: 6px;
}

/* --------------------------------------------------------- ProgressBar */

/* The "People's Progress" -- red filling on a dark groove. */
QProgressBar {
    border: 1px solid #3A3A3A;
    background-color: #0D0D0D;
    text-align: center;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    font-weight: bold;
}

QProgressBar::chunk {
    background-color: #D95231;
    margin: 1px;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------- Misc chrome */

QLabel {
    background: transparent;
    color: #F2E4C4;
}

QLabel:disabled {
    color: #6E6E6E;
}

QSplitter::handle {
    background-color: #161616;
}

QSplitter::handle:hover {
    background-color: #D4AF37;
}

QScrollBar:vertical {
    background: #2A2A28;
    width: 16px;
    border: 1px solid #3A3A3A;
}

QScrollBar::handle:vertical {
    background-color: #3A3A3A;
    border: 1px solid #0D0D0D;
    min-height: 24px;
}

QScrollBar::handle:vertical:hover {
    background-color: #D95231;
}

QScrollBar::add-line:vertical, QScrollBar::sub-line:vertical {
    height: 0px;
    background: none;
    border: none;
}

QScrollBar::add-page:vertical, QScrollBar::sub-page:vertical {
    background: none;
}

QScrollBar:horizontal {
    background: #2A2A28;
    height: 16px;
    border: 1px solid #3A3A3A;
}

QScrollBar::handle:horizontal {
    background-color: #3A3A3A;
    border: 1px solid #0D0D0D;
    min-width: 24px;
}

QScrollBar::handle:horizontal:hover {
    background-color: #D95231;
}

QScrollBar::add-line:horizontal, QScrollBar::sub-line:horizontal {
    width: 0px;
    background: none;
    border: none;
}

QScrollBar::add-page:horizontal, QScrollBar::sub-page:horizontal {
    background: none;
}

QSizeGrip {
    background-color: #161616;
    width: 16px;
    height: 16px;
}

QToolTip {
    background-color: #2A2A28;
    color: #F2E4C4;
    border: 2px solid #D95231;
    border-radius: 0px;
    padding: 4px 6px;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Propaganda side panel (src/torrent2000/ui/widgets/propaganda_panel.py)
   -- the extra strip of window width shown only under this theme.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

QWidget#cccpPropagandaPanel {
    background-color: #0D0D0D;
    border-left: 4px solid #D95231;
}

QLabel#propagandaHeader {
    color: #D95231;
    font-weight: bold;
    font-size: 10pt;
}

QLabel#propagandaMessage {
    color: #F2E4C4;
    font-size: 9pt;
}

QFrame#propagandaDivider {
    background-color: #D4AF37;
    border: none;
}
